Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: apps/ca.c
Line: 1661
Function: certify
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: BIO_printf is invoked with the %s formatter using ASN1_STRING->data from str/str2, which are not guaranteed to be NUL-terminated. This can cause a read past the end of the allocated buffer until a NUL byte is encountered: BIO_printf(bio_err, ..., ((str2 == NULL) ? "NULL" : (char *)str2->data), ((str == NULL) ? "NULL" : (char *)str->data));. If a policy 'match' fails, attacker-controlled ASN1 string data from the request/issuer can trigger this OOB read, leading to a crash or information leak.

